WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:08.600
Before Kano was a city, it was a hill. People worked iron on Dala.

2
00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:13.400
The Kano Chronicle remembers Barbushe, keeper of a shrine on the hill. That memory is tradition, and it has no date.

3
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:19.600
By the Chronicle's reckoning, King Gijimasu began a wall, gate by gate.

4
00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:24.600
Who finished it? The Chronicle says Yusa, in the 1100s. Nigeria's heritage file says Zamnagawa, in the 1300s.

5
00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:29.400
Then Muhammad Rumfa. The Chronicle says he built a palace and moved in the next year.

6
00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:34.600
The year after, he pushed the walls outward, gate by gate.

7
00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:38.600
He founded a market, Kurmi, which still trades today.

8
00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:43.000
A scholar, al-Maghili, wrote Rumfa a book on how a king should rule.

9
00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:47.600
A walled city needs more than walls. Who lived inside them?
